Z||000008||Jay||07-26-2001||02:23 PM||||Grinthock...sucks to be you <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I wanna see tons of Americans there.  We all go to Michigan, I hope they return the favour! CanadianGT I might be persuaded to give you a ride in the Northstar...make me an offer I can't refuse!<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||grinthock||07-26-2001||08:51 PM||||Jay;<P>   I wanted to go, infact I was one of the people who spoke with the organizers about moving the show because of Georgio's wedding.  But now I am being told by the GTA club President that I am not welcome in the club, at any meetings or at the show, and that the show organizers do not want me there either.  Last year I got up at 5am and didn't goto bed till 11pm as I helped run the show.  <P><BR>    I was basically told at the end of the conversation that I am to receive the same treatment as the RSM guys.<P><BR>    I do'nt see why entrace to the show is for selected people only, I mean just because the president has a personal tiff with me shouldn't exclude me from the show, apparantly the GTA club has turned the show into a show for people in the "Clique" only, if you are not one of the "popular" Fiero owners in the GTA area and part of their group you end up being excluded, Tim Lester was told last year he is not allowed back because he boycotted the GTA club because of personal feelings from another member, and then the organizers told him he wasn't welcome back.<P>   WHY is the group split?  WHY do those of us outside have to put up with this?  It's this kind of thing that destory's clubs as it is doing to the GTA club.  <P>  I dunno the whole situation is stupid, and I can't fix it, and I do'nt think this should go un0heard anymore.<P>    NO!! This is not a flame thread but a Controversey thread, and do'nt start flaming here guys it's not the point.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jay||07-27-2001||07:29 AM||||The point is that you have made several remarks about the club to people.  Some of those remarks were offensive.  I don't want to start flaming you but I think that from what you have said, you shot yourself in the foot.  As far as Tim and RSM that was different.  RSM is not welcome to the show as a company.  It only makes sense that the sponsors of the show not be undermined by another company who doesn't sponsor the show.  In otherwords RSM was getting free publicity and handing out business cards at a show that they didn't organize or pay for.  Their customers on the other hand are more than welcome if they pay the fee and DON"T HAND OUT CARDS.  Tim was told not to hand out RSM business cards and yet he still did.  That is why he is not welcome (as well as a whole bunch of other stuff which we will not get into here)<P>When you make comments about the club, about it's president and about people who belong to the club I and others take it seriously.  We don't see it as a clique, we see it as weeding out people who are trouble makers.  If you disagree with me, read the threads on FieroLisa, Joe Trentadue and others in which you attack people for no valid reason.  You get yourself into trouble.  We want a good vibe in the club and you don't have to be popular to be welcome, just follow some simple rules.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Adrift||07-27-2001||08:08 PM||||I don't really see a reason to attend a Fiero show - I don't really go to car shows in General. I mean, I don't really get excited looking at other peoples cars (and I wouldn't pay for the privledge). I could see them being very useful to find customizing info/parts/see what others are doing, but this forum provides me with my daily fix of all the above. What other reasons are there for attending this fiero show?||||reg||1
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||07-27-2001||09:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Adrift:<BR><B>I don't really see a reason to attend a Fiero show - I don't really go to car shows in General. I mean, I don't really get excited looking at other peoples cars (and I wouldn't pay for the privledge). I could see them being very useful to find customizing info/parts/see what others are doing, but this forum provides me with my daily fix of all the above. What other reasons are there for attending this fiero show?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One of the things I like best about Fiero shows, is meeting people that I've talked to online, as well as new Fiero people.. also, seeing cars in person that I've seen pics of online.. eg. Jay's Northstar GT.... that car kicks ass.......<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jay||07-27-2001||09:42 PM||||thanks for the compliment Darklord.  Adrift, it is free to come and look at the cars and meet people, you don't have to pay for that.  You only have to pay to enter the show with your car.  The benefits of entering are having your car judged.  Winning a trophy and rubbing it in someones face <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> just kidding!  But it really is fun to hang out all day and talk fiero junk and meet new people.  So even if you don't enter your car come out and see us!<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||72vinman||07-27-2001||10:29 PM||||I will be there for sure. It is being held less than 5 minutes away from my place. I am going to look at an 86GT tomorrow morning. So if all goes well I will be at the show with my very on GT. I look forward to meeting all of you from the forum.||||reg||10
Z||000015||grinthock||07-27-2001||11:05 PM||||Jay;<P>    This isn't meant to be a flamewar -- I do'nt condone those, the issue here is how the president has a PERSONAL problem with me.  I have never had a problem with him.  So I made some controversial comments in the FL thread, and the Joe thread I spoke my experience, how is that a crime?  Are we trying to HIDE the truth?  NOBODY ELSE is willing to admit the truths that *I* brought out in the joe thread.  All I said was they were hard to get ahold of....  As for TIM, he does not WORK for RSM he is a customer.  He was NOT going around the show handing out cards.  One guy ASKED and he gave that guy one, someone saw and said "RSM isn't sponsoring this, Race-Tech Is, so please do'nt hand out cards"  So he didn't sit there handing them out.   Infact he didn't hand out even one more.<P>I do'nt see what rules you are talking about, ok so I can't hand out rival shop cards..... What rules have I BROKEN that now I can not attend the show like everyone else?  As for the club and the remarks?  I havn't made remarks about the club other than the meetings WERE getting boring (Which they WERE at that time, I hear they are better) and I can't make it up tuesdays for the meetings now so that doesn't matter.  I TRIED to be proactive and do the newsletter and NOBODY offered to help.   All I said was the club was getting boring and there were certain people there who were ruining it for others.    *I* just happen to be the ONLY person who talks about it.<P>What's with this secret society anyway!?  People all talk in riddles, talk in groups, I tried SO HARD to push the club when I was with a group of 8 other fiero owners who said "The club sucks now, I can't stand it" and some of them mentioned names, which I won't.<P><BR>That's about all my thoughts right now.... <P>Anyone OUTSIDE the situation wanna comment on why I shouldn't be allowed?  If it's because of this thread, I made the comments because "The president of the GTA Fiero Club has a PERSONAL tiff with me and now has BANNED me from the show"<P><BR>EVERYTHING I have said here in the joe thread and here in this thread have been said by NUMEROUS others.... And you and everyone else in the club knows it --- I am just the person who brings it out in the open......  <P><p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Jay||07-27-2001||11:59 PM||||Actually Justin (Grinthock), YOU have a problem with the president of the club.  Calling him a "spoiled little jew boy" amongst other comments sent you out of the club.  As for the newsletter, remember I was the editor before you.  I volunteered several articles which didn't appear in the newsletter you did, which is fine...but don't *****  that nobody helped out.  I have several more articles waiting to be printed in the newsletter by our new editor.  Maybe nobody else wants to admitt the truth because the truth is not how you percieve it to be.  Why is it that you are the only one we have banned?  The decision was not made soley by the president but was voted on.  To be honest, I believe that the vote was not to allow you to be in the club NOT that you couldn't attend the show, I'll check the minutes and get back to you on that.  Bottom line...we don't want people that will stir things up amongst members, take that as you will.  But when you speak badly about the club you speak badly of me personally, because I am part of that club.  If you feel you've been mistreated, than speak to our president.  With the remarks you made to the president I'm surprised he didn't kick your a$$, because if you said that stuff about me I would be tempted to.  Justin, you are a good guy but I think sometimes you say things without thinking of what the consequences of your words will be.  Think before you speak (or type), and things like this will be avoided.  That's all I have to say about this.  Back to the topic...who's comming?||||reg||1
Z||000017||grinthock||07-29-2001||06:52 PM||||Now what you are saying is now Hearsay.... At NO TIME did I say anything RACIAL to him, neither spoken nor written/typed.  Why would I?  I put up with enough of that being a person of Jewish decent in the first place....<P><BR>Let's see, the club meeting where you guys voted on that who was represented?   First, Race-Tech Fiero Shop, who now have a tiff with me (personal), the president who doesn't like me because I joked about him backing his car into a pole a year ago, and he has never let it go not to mention whenever you talk fieros with him his response is "I am selling it and driving a REAL car"  I have personally heard him say that on NUMEROUS occasions, so have others, Lothar, BanditBalz and others.<BR> <P>AS for the newsletter, you can take this back to the club, I worked my ASS off designing a new format, new design for it, if you look ALL the articles in that issue (excluding I beleive one) were MY OWN.  Yes you did offer some, and they were slated for the next issue, which I was 1 month behind on because NOBODY sent me squat, in FACT the president didn't send me the stuff he had received even after MYSELF and the club secretary BUGGED him like mad... WHY?  Because HE didn't want to deal with me.<P>Anyone who has a problem with the club should email me directly at my listed email address I will explain other various issues.  But I have had it.  <P>Personally, anyone who has PAID for a GTA club membership should immediatly request a REFUND, they promised everyone a newsletter, 4 a year in fact and they didn't come through, so request a refund, you deserve it, if not a refund at least a "re-imbursement" either in Cash or towards next years renewal.<P>As for the show, I will be there, regardless of weather or not I am allowed/invited.  In the parking lot with the rest of those who have been "Banned" from the GTA club, currently my count is up to 8 people.  So for all those out there who voted for GTA as the club with the best "Participation" and one of the "best" clubs around, think again, because THIS member was banned because of politics and because the president is a im-mature person who can not segregate personal problems from club/business issues.<P>I NEVER had problems while at the club/meetings/show or otherwise.  I had a PERSONAL tiff with him only.<P>Let me see if I get this right.<P>1)  The club gets togeather<P>2)  The president (Noticed how names here havn't been mentioned!) said he is pissed at me because of a "supposed" comment<P>3)  The RACE-TECH club sponsor was there and was miffed because I happend to mention I was ticked at them on PFF<P>4)  So They decided, "Well none of us like the guy", so those people (who represent probably 1/4 --&gt; 1/3 of those attending) decide to vote me out because they had a PERSONAL problem.<P>Tell me if I am wrong.  Why should I be extridited from a NON PROFIT club that I didn't cause ONE problem AT.  I actually enjoyed the meetings when I was there, but myself (Like MANY OTHER who REFUSE to speak out, unlike myself), have had it with the politics and hearing about how the sponsor HATES certain people, and how the president can't stand certain people.<P><BR>I also enjoy how NOBODY from the area is willing to back me here, why don't you guys stand up for what you know is right!?  Or do guys all want to stay in the background as usual?  Come on guys, give me some support here, it's about time we fixed the problems this club has had.<P>Suggestions?<P>1)  REMOVE the integration of the major sponsor with the club, it's too inter-twined<P>2)  NONE of the major sponsor's STAFF should be in the executive<P>3)  Invite other Fiero businesses into the club circle<P>4)  GET PROACTIVE!  Everyone has to cast their vote for the executive otherwise all this will crumble.<P><BR>All you guys complained about the club, I said "Let's start a niagra region club" and nobody wants to split the group up, I CAN'T AGREE MORE!! Let's keep it all togeather but for that to work there has to be some compromise.   Some giving from both sides, meaning those who don't like to drive 30 minutes to a club meeting -- TOO BAD!!  Some of us have been doing it for a LONG TIME!! Why not share the responsibility, some of you guys do it, so we can only drive 10-15.<P>I want ONE unified club here (Geez bill gates and that damn unified word, next thing you know I will be getting nailed for Anti-Trust) with ONE group, because togeather we can all be bigger than any club around.<P><BR>That's all I got, my fingers hurt.... Gnight<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Jay||07-29-2001||07:17 PM||||First off, it is the GTA (Greater Toronto area) club, not the Oakville club or the Niagara club or the Burlington club.  I drive over a half an hour to get to the meetings and I have never complained!  It's a car club damn it!  what is wrong with driving your car?!?!?!<P>The reason Race-Tech is so entwined with the club is because Joe and Mirriame along with a few others were doing all of the work!  Yes you volunteered but the majority of the time there are 4-5 people doing everything!  If Race tech was not involved in the club then nothing would get done, that is a fact.<P>You make it sound like you didn't do anything wrong, when in fact you are a trouble maker, plain and simple.  Why incite people to quit the club and ask for a refund?  The newsletter is being produced as we speak!  Why is it that the new editor has everything he needs for the next issue?  Why is it that you continually tried to get people to break off from the GTA club?  I don't use any names because very few of the people who have issues with you use this board and I don't want to violate anyones privacy.  You brought this up.  I only asked who was coming.  <P>You say 8 people have been banned?  Who?  RSM as a company has been banned for what happened last year.  They have been sent legal notices not to attend, because we don't want any trouble.  The club is being very reasonable about this situation.  It is not fair to Race Tech to have to share publicity with a former business partner who has done nothing for the club.<BR>  The attendence at the meeting which banned you was about 20 people.  As far as I can see Race tech only has 2 members and the president and vice president are another 2 people, that's 4.  Where is the conspiracy?  If what you say is true, that vote should never have passed.  You have also been quoted by many people making bad remarks about the club to your Burlington boys, don't act all innocent!  Like I said we don't want a trouble maker in the club.  Stop and listen to what you say.  Like I said, you're alright but you speak without listening to yourself.<P>Nobody has stepped up because you are wrong, plain and simple.  Yes it is a non profit organization, but without Race Tech it would crumble.  We have several sponsors, for one Stereo Dimension.  Now how would they feel after sponsoring us for so long if we invited another stereo company to sponsor us at the show?  Or Steve's tire.  We wouldn't go and ask Wheels Direct to come to the show would we?  Of coarse not, and that is a major reason why RSM is not invited as a company.  Their clients are more than welcome to attend if they follow the rules.<P>If you want to respond start your own thread.<P>Now who else is coming?||||reg||1
Z||000019||Slammed Fiero||07-29-2001||07:47 PM||||I just read through all this BS<P>Justin..What about the time you threatened to get "Satans Choice" to come to beat me up because they owe you a favour?? Because I said something against you?<P>Or how about the time you flew off the handle because I touched a switch in your car and it blew a fuse? 4 people witnessed that extravaganza of stupidity.<P>Or!!! The time you got all pissy at me because I come from a wealthy family, you told me your sob story of how you pay for everything. You have something against people with money , were not as good as you?? I  know thats why you don't like the president, because he comes from a wealthy family. I mean I have had my probs with him 2 , we both grew up , and go to school together at georgian, I see and talk to him everyday. The little punk wakes me up with the GTI every morning driving past my residence room.<P>Your acting like a spoiled little kid , waiting for people to come to your rescue because of the "injustice" that has been committed against you. <P>Just grow up , plain and simple. <P>You wanted an outside view?? I have been to 1 GTA show in 5 years and 1 meeting. And I'm NOT a member of the GTA club.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000020||grinthock||07-29-2001||09:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR>[B]First off, it is the GTA (Greater Toronto area) club, not the Oakville club or the Niagara club or the Burlington club.  I drive over a half an hour to get to the meetings and I have never complained!  It's a car club damn it!  what is wrong with driving your car?!?!?!  <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I do'nt have a problem at all!  Infact the location is GREAT For me as I work up in that area, however MANY people from west Toronto and Niagra have asked if we could OCCASIONALLY move it. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><P>The reason Race-Tech is so entwined with the club is because Joe and Mirriame along with a few others were doing all of the work!  Yes you volunteered but the majority of the time there are 4-5 people doing everything!  If Race tech was not involved in the club then nothing would get done, that is a fact.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ABSOLUTLY this is a fact!  I couldn't agree more, that's why my previous msg is telling people they MUST get invovled for the goodness of the club.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>You make it sound like you didn't do anything wrong, when in fact you are a trouble maker, plain and simple.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How am I a trouble maker?  Because I told everyone that I was banned because (again) a personal tiff?<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>  Why incite people to quit the club and ask for a refund?  The newsletter is being produced as we speak!  Why is it that the new editor has everything he needs for the next issue? <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Because until you guys didn't HAVE one at all nobody would contribute, that's what happened last time, when we BEGGED stuff came in, once one issue published I got NOTHING.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR> Why is it that you continually tried to get people to break off from the GTA club?  <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Because the idea was BROUGHT TO ME by various WESTERN niagra members who said they wouldn't mind starting something here because THEY (not I) didn't want to drive and they had some issues with the club.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>I don't use any names because very few of the people who have issues with you use this board and I don't want to violate anyones privacy. <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Obviously this was a mis-communication, I wasn't suggesting you were using names, I was just pointing out that I wasn't going to use names, sorry Jay.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>You say 8 people have been banned?  Who?<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Names are not appropriate here.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>  RSM as a company has been banned for what happened last year.  They have been sent legal notices not to attend, because we don't want any trouble.  The club is being very reasonable about this situation.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What?  Because ONE member decided to enter the show with a RSM sticker?  I know about those letters last year and I protested at the meeting, and I know other members thought it was stupid too.  The club is taking it too far.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>  It is not fair to Race Tech to have to share publicity with a former business partner who has done nothing for the club.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree but someone's stickers shouldn't decide WHO can and who CAN'T be in the show, there was someone ELSE at the show NOT sponsoring the show (actually 3 individuals, 1 of which READS PENNOCKS) who were handing out cards too, I have one of them, but I am not bringing up his name, I APPRICIATE the card because I speak with that individual OFTEN now.  It was a great contact.  As for people giving out RSM cards?  what's wrong if someone ASKS for it, Tims was not OFFERING the cards, people ASKED him for one, and I witnessed that.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>  The attendence at the meeting which banned you was about 20 people.  As far as I can see Race tech only has 2 members and the president and vice president are another 2 people, that's 4.  Where is the conspiracy?  If what you say is true, that vote should never have passed.  <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not without the coercion, if they were coerced into thinking that I was doing something I wasn't then they may have voted against me, that's being guilty without defending myself.  Had I known that you had staged a "vote" against me, I would have been there.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>You have also been quoted by many people making bad remarks about the club to your Burlington boys, don't act all innocent! <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Bad remarks how?  Because I had a problem with the pres?  Because he was supposed to send me information for the newsletter and didn't?  How the meetings I went to had 6 people in them?  I didn't BASH anything, BASHING would mean I said something NOT true, which I did not.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR> Like I said we don't want a trouble maker in the club.  Stop and listen to what you say.  Like I said, you're alright but you speak without listening to yourself.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hardly!  I listen to what I am saying and other than being truthful and outspoken I have nothing wrong.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>Nobody has stepped up because you are wrong, plain and simple.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No it's because certiain people who again I wo'nt mention names refuse to come out of the political MESS for fear of reprisal by the club, MORE BANNING!<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>  Yes it is a non profit organization, but without Race Tech it would crumble.  We have several sponsors, for one Stereo Dimension. <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I didn't know they were a sponsor that must be new.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR> Now how would they feel after sponsoring us for so long if we invited another stereo company to sponsor us at the show?<BR>  Or Steve's tire.  We wouldn't go and ask Wheels Direct to come to the show would we?  Of coarse not, and that is a major reason why RSM is not invited as a company.  Their clients are more than welcome to attend if they follow the rules.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I couldn't agree with you more, as I have said AGAIN and AGAIN!  This isn't the brunt of my arugement here.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>If you want to respond start your own thread.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Why so AGAIN the truth's of the GTA club can get hidden in the redderick of politics?  No way.  I am not dropping this.<BR>||||reg||1
